{
  "id": "learning-switch",
  "name": "How a Switch Learns",
  "category": "switching",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "xp": 150,
  "level": 4,
  "description": "Watch a switch build its MAC address table from nothing.",
  "brief": "A switch starts life knowing nothing. It learns where each machine lives by reading the source address of every frame that arrives, and it floods anything it has not learned yet out of every port.\n\nOpen Switch-01's terminal and run 'show mac-address-table' before you do anything: it is empty. Then ping between the PCs and watch the table fill up, and the flooding stop.\n\nComplete the mission by getting all three PCs talking.",
  "hints": [
    "Switch-01 > show mac-address-table",
    "PC-01 > ping 10.20.0.13",
    "Run the table command again. Two entries appeared.",
    "Watch the event log: the first frame floods, later ones do not."
  ],
